WEBVTT

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.350
In a universe somewhere

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.520
is a galaxy somewhere...

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.110
Within which somewhere is a planet:

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.900
Earthdash.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:16.620
There, when you look up at the sky,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.200
you see a city called Mooneyes on the face of the moon.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.540
Brighter than the sun during the day,

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.880
and shining more beautifully than the stars at night,

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:32.470
it is a symbol for the hopes and dreams of the people.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.550
They all dream of someday living on the moon...

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.930
You became a legend.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.830
I-I'm a legend?

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:03.700
LEGEND IS DEAD

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.670
You know, as a general rule, streetball isn't allowed during the middle of the day.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:19.850
Keep it down! You woke up my kid!

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.100
I'm calling the cops!

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.470
Sorry!

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.100
You're the one who started this trend.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.020
Huh?

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:30.110
I guess seeing you play opened the eyes of all the Bigfoot operators.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.860
I wanted to crush Bigfoot Basketball.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.440
That's all.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.030
See? Look how popular you are.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:40.510
It's Dan!

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.740
It's Dunk Mask!

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.790
Give me your autograph!

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.580
Me too!

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.120
Hey, hey! I have nothing to write with!

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.790
Hey, don't pull on that!

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.670
Even if you ask, it's not like I can...

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.460
Hey! I told you not to pull! Knock it off, that hurts!

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.670
Here you go, Dunk Mask.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.110
Oh, a marker!

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:57.800
It's permanent!

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.730
You can sign with that!

00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:00.340
Give us your autograph!

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.110
Come on, please!

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.750
Okay! You got me.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.310
I'll give it to you!

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.310
Yay!

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:06.900
I'm first, okay?

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.770
Sign right here!

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:08.770
Here you go!

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:09.940
All right!

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.810
Thanks!

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:14.860
How's that?

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.610
Awesome! Thanks!

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.700
Bye! See you later!

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:21.990
Thanks for the marker—

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.730
That match that destroyed the stadium...

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.000
I had a great time.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.700
Well, here's your marker—

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.830
Here, to celebrate your release.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.420
Let's meet again, Legend.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.000
Huh?

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.460
H-Hey, your marker!

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.590
Want my autograph?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:42.930
Idiot.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.720
Here we go, the heart-warming brother-sister reunion.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:46.930
Don't cry, Dan.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.600
Shut up!

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.900
Coming.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.820
Y-Yo. I'm home!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.860
Sorry to take so long... I mean, yeah, right?!

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.580
Oh these? I don't really know, but this weird fan of mine gave me flowers... I mean, no!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.580
Your older brother bought them for you of course!

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.330
Should I autograph you too? Haha!

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.420
I don't need this marker, do I?

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.380
How time flies, you know?

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.420
Before I noticed, it was like one, two, three... a year!

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.460
It's been a year!

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:23.050
But sheesh! Make just a little ruckus and the adults gang up on you; they can't take a joke at all.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.180
But that's how the world works, right?

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.970
And your brother never lets that get him down!

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:31.310
While in my cell, my thoughts were always of you, Coco!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.020
I wondered, "What's Coco's doing now? Did she eat dinner?"

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.980
"Did she brush her teeth?"

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.570
"Did she do her homework? Did she take a bath?"

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.030
Like, "Same time next week!" right? {sz: I think he's riffing on the next episode previews for like, soap operas or something.}

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:41.610
Hey, listen!

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:44.240
I'm sorry I made things tough on you, but it's okay now!

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:47.080
From now on we'll work together like a real brother and sister—

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:47.740
What's that?

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:48.620
From City Hall.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.750
"Bill"?

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:55.540
Destruction of the stadium, halting the event, cancellation fees to the different stations, et cetera.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.920
Ones, tens, hundreds, thousands...

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.920
"Totaling 5.3 billion rollings," they said.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.180
Billion?!

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.050
I had nothing to do with this.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.470
W-Wait a second, Coco!

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.850
You may not have been watching, but your brother did it!

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.770
He became a legend!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.860
A legend even though he missed the dunk.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.910
Coco! Open up, c'mon!

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:30.370
Just because you're the sister of a legend, you don't have to be shy, you know! C'mon!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.700
Hey, little dumpling! How have you been?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.290
Coco...

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.880
Don't worry! I'll ride on your head again!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.880
Man, you've got a legend-worthy debt too.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.130
Well, don't give up. Get a part-time job or something.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.640
What, you're going home?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.470
Well, look.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.100
You can't get into the Legend's room.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.270
Let's hang out again, Legend.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.330
What's wrong, brother?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.340
Shut up!

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.670
Oh, Coco, your shoelace—

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.500
What?

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.380
Mine now!

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.800
That's no fair!

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.260
Just you watch, Coco!

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:31.930
Your brother's gonna make the most tripped-out, extreme dunk right here, right now!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.940
You suck so bad!

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:53.330
It hurts!

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.620
Coco!

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:58.710
What about her legs? When are they gonna heal, huh?!

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.590
We can reassemble the shattered bones.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.510
But there's nothing we can do about the shredded nerves.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.550
Nothing... You mean...

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.680
I mean it's no use hoping.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.140
No use?! You call yourself a doctor?!

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.930
You better do something, and do it now!

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:14.560
Coco...

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.770
Coco, you know...

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.310
She's way better than me at basketball,

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.770
and she's way cooler than me,

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.610
and compared to me... to some punk like me...

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.810
she's got such a brilliant future as a player!

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:26.690
Please...

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.820
Please!

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.700
Don't take basketball away from her...

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.030
The moon.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:35.870
The moon?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.250
I doubt she'll ever be healed with the medical facilities available here,

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.540
but if she went to the moon, there's hope...

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:43.040
Can her legs be healed if she goes to the moon?!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:47.380
On the moon, medical science is much more advanced than it is here.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.130
There is a definite possibility.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:06.920
watashi wa tsuki kara maiorita usagi

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:06.920
I'm the rabbit that came from the moon

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:12.530
mirai wo watashi ni kiita no

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:12.530
to bring you the future.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:18.220
jibun wo jibun ni kaeru ticket

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:18.220
A ticket that transforms you into your true self yourself.

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.980
moon passport

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:21.980
A moon passport.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.280
ah~ kudaranai mainichi wo

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.280
Ah~ Take the petty, soulless daily grind

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:33.690
itsuwari no jiyuu wa kowashite

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:33.690
and the false freedom, and shatter them.

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:40.650
mada minu keshiki ga mune wo hiraku

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:40.650
An unseen vista will appear and let you breathe again.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:46.300
atarashii densetsu wo eien no mirai wo

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:46.300
So carve a new legend in the distant future

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:51.880
mada furenu sekai e kizamu

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:51.880
in the world we have yet to explore.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:08:02.340
massara de dokidoki no tokimeita heart ni kiss wo shite

00:07:51.880 --> 00:08:02.340
This new feeling, my heart is racing... Kiss me.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.460
kiss wo shite-

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.460
Kiss me now-

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:21.270
You think maybe I could get to the moon in that machine?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.810
Getting there or not is up to you.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.860
Welcome back, Dan.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:33.990
"Dunk Mask comes home saddled with huge debt"?!

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:35.740
Huh? Where's that one?

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:40.040
Let's see, "Formerly imprisoned for the crime of destroying the Rolling Arena,

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.870
Boy A, known as Dunk Mask, has been released."

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.410
"With a bill from Rollingtown for the incredible sum of..."

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.000
Five point...

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:46.500
...three...

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.000
...billion...

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.130
...rollings?!

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:53.340
"The boy, carrying a debt on a national scale,

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:58.260
which could hardly be paid back in ten lifetimes, appears to have been thrown out of his house.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:02.450
"What effect will this have on the current state of Bigfoot Streetball?

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:03.850
This reporter can hardly wait.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.350
Ultimate Bystander, signing off."

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.810
Sounds tough.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.530
That man...

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:16.040
Debt? Thrown out?!

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.280
Bastard makes it sound like he was there!

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.830
What if he was?

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:27.620
Let's see... "What effect will this have on the current state of Bigfoot Streetball"...

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.460
Hey, what's Bigfoot Streetball?

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.630
It's the Bigfoot Basketball style that's so hot right now.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.590
That, huh?

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.340
Well, if you ask old legendary me, they've got a ways to go.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.280
Who do you think you are?

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.440
Oh no! Thief!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.010
Catch him!

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.350
You, on that bike... S-Stop!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.270
Sorry, um, excuse me...

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.650
Coming through!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.780
Pardon me.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:52.670
You moron!

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:54.320
Please let me through...

00:09:55.860 --> 00:10:00.240
Idiot. Why waste your time wading through a traffic jam?

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.580
So he should run on the wall like you or something?

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.870
That's it!

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.120
How is it?

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.790
It's good!

00:10:07.790 --> 00:10:08.580
What?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:12.420
It's the new business venture I've made for you.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:13.420
Don't yank my chain!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.880
What's the big idea dragging them into it too?

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.130
What's wrong with that?

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.050
We're all childhood friends, right?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:20.970
Yup!

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.850
Like old times!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.930
We used to all play together a lot, remember?

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.520
But I never expected this!

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.900
She used to be such a crybaby, but after Dan was arrested last year...

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:35.190
...Miyuki came home all grown up!

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.570
Enough with the reminiscing, okay?

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:41.360
More importantly, what do you plan to do with this?

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.700
A delivery service. Door-to-door!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.870
Door-to-door delivery... You mean me?!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:50.410
Right! You can test his legs by running all over town.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:54.750
It'll also serve as advertisement for our maintenance service and earn money. Three birds with one stone!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.050
Sorry, but I've got no reason to play along.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.840
You want to go to the moon, don't you?

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:02.090
So you've gotta succeed, no matter what.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:05.850
Whether it's a job or something else, the one who stands out the most wins.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.020
All right then!

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:10.770
Oh nice!

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.900
I can run as much as I have to with this!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.980
Hey! Deliver something for me!

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.360
Yes, sir! Right away, sir!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.570
Hear that? Our first customer!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:21.200
R-Right!

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.030
Any destination is just a leap away for Dunk Mask's Dangan Delivery!

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:26.200
Thanks for your—

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:35.000
Hey! That made the debt go <i>up</i>, not down!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.170
What are you going to do about this?

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.630
I knew a machine wasn't gonna cut it!

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.300
That's not the problem!

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.590
It's just your crude handling!

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.800
What do you mean crude?!

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.510
<i>You're</i> just your big tits!

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:46.930
Maybe Miyuki's right, Dan.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:51.560
Some structures can withstand the weight, others can't.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.620
I think you can run through town just fine if we plan out some routes.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.260
You know a lot about buildings, son?

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:02.240
If it's standing in Rollingtown, I know everything from Town Hall down to the doghouses.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.780
I want to be an architect when I grow up.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:08.490
So that just leaves the Bigfoot...

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:10.870
We can whip something up.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:12.330
I've had enough of this.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.120
You. Don't you want to heal Coco's legs?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.260
Hey! How's it going?

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.670
It sucks!

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:25.130
But where were you all this time anyway, you jerk?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.680
I heard "delivery service" and remembered these.

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:32.350
Thought I'd hire you for a delivery myself.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:33.890
What are those?

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:36.400
Are these... sandals?

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.690
Yeah! I cut them from old tires.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.650
They're my greatest invention!

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:43.820
And they sell like hotcakes at construction sites!

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:47.660
I got another order so I thought I'd have you deliver them.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.410
This is it!

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:58.170
Got it. This is the shipment, correct?

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.670
Fill out your address and the shipping address on that form.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:01.960
Welcome!

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.340
For large items we will arrange pickup from your door!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:08.090
We've already got as many orders as we can handle.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:12.720
If you don't mind waiting several days, write your name and address here.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.440
It'll be week after next.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:19.980
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.480
The red roof three buildings down from there.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:26.450
From that house, all of the rooftops connect in a straight line, so just keep going.

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:27.860
Roger!

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:30.700
What's that?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.370
It's wearing sandals!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.590
Mama! It's running on the roofs!

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:38.490
Don't stare!

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.960
They all look at me and do a double take.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.260
They're looking at the Bigfoot, not you.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.170
Shut up!

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:48.090
No other human could run like this!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.180
What manufacturer are you from?

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:56.640
You came down from the moon, didn't you?

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.020
N-No!

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:00.150
Don't try to hide it. I can tell by looking at you.

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.860
You just got here?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:04.190
You're shaky on your feet in this gravity.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.360
Why don't you quit sneaking around over here...

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.210
...and take pictures in full daylight up close?

00:14:10.210 --> 00:14:10.740
Huh?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:14.040
Technology thrives best when it's being shared.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.410
However, <i>technique</i> is a personal thing.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.250
<i>That</i> you can't steal so easily.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.540
Th-Thank you very much!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.040
My company is lagging behind and this will— {barfing sounds}

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:27.630
Careful. If you look down, your food is likely to come back up.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:28.710
You're gravity-sick. {sz: like the opposite of being spacesick I guess}

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.340
Is that okay?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:33.100
If they manage to get a patent or something, aren't they stealing from you?

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.310
Well, my family is like that.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.600
That's why Gramps and Dad both came down from there.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:46.400
Dad!

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.490
And that's why I won't let it beat me either.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.860
Not ever.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:54.950
Excellent!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.660
I'm gonna conquer the world with this thing!

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.370
And then straight on to the moon!

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:02.210
Just you wait, Coco!

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:07.010
Lately, we've been hearing people talking about him all the time.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:11.720
Well, right now he really is working hard.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.100
How does it feel to make a legend into your personal carrier boy?

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.680
Does it make you feel superior? In a sadistic way?

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.930
I don't have to answer that.

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:21.730
Don't take me wrong.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.940
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.690
One of these days I'll get my chance to have my fill of him.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.150
Dan hates your type, I'm afraid.

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:33.360
I thought you were the one who hates me.

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:37.780
In the end, you know,
 men like women with technique.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:42.040
Well, I hope that technique works out for you.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.790
Exactly. I'll clip his wings for you. {lol so many notes. This phrase is literally "debone" or "water down" (or "emasculate") and it means to remove the most essential part of something. Alt tl is maybe "I'll take the wind out of his sails for you" but I don't think that's strong enough.}

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:57.350
Hey, Bel.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.510
What?

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.930
The side mirror's cracked.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.610
Oh, that's so you can look at the Bigfoot's feet.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:08.320
Miyuki comes up with some pretty neat stuff.

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.150
Yes.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:12.700
Our delivery waiting list is full for two months, but you'd still like to be placed on it?

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.780
Yes, that's right.

00:16:12.940 --> 00:16:15.570
And everyone and their brother wants to copy us.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:15.720
Yes, of course. {continues unintelligibly}

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:16.410
What's wrong with that?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:19.950
It's great when things become easier to use for everyone.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.500
Yeah, sure.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.670
But you know what? Only I can do this!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:28.040
You're the only idiot who would!

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.000
This is the pace of a legend!

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:35.050
What the?!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.890
Smart-ass!

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.310
He's better than you are.

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:44.020
Shut up!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.020
Wait up, you!

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:47.110
Hey! What about the delivery?

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:48.360
I can't let this go!

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.190
Why?

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:51.320
Because he copied your business plan?

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.070
No!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.440
Those feet and sandals...

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:57.490
Do Miyuki and Ganz take orders from any jerk who's a customer?!

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:58.490
Jealous?

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.830
Shut up!

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.830
Oh, hey. Look at that.

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:06.920
It's Dunk Mask. What's he doing?

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.920
The other one... That's Platinum Hurricane!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:13.250
Dammit!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.930
A... A woman?

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:21.180
Sela Miranda!

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.390
That's right. It's Platinum Hurricane, Sela Miranda!

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:27.690
"C'mon and chase me," huh?

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:28.900
Okay then!

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:30.060
Hey, Dunk Mask!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.730
Use that!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.740
Right!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.430
Sorry, but could you deliver this?

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.700
You won't beat my running and you won't beat my dribbling!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.330
I'm the legendary Dunk Mask!

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:45.190
Platinum Delivery!

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:51.920
Dammit, dammit.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.090
Dammit!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:17:59.550
Shit!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.650
Hey! Where'd you go?

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.320
Wha—

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:24.950
Why you!

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.080
What are you trying to—

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:30.670
One-on-one, huh?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:31.580
You got it!

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:36.670
You bitch!

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:53.230
Like hell I will!

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:56.520
Higher! Higher!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.370
Shit! That woman!

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.670
What a wimp, losing to a girl...

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.590
Oh, you don't get it.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.510
Man, woman, that has nothing to with it.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:20.170
What?

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:23.720
As Crawly said. Being a man or a woman is beside the point.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:27.390
With Bigfoots, it's the person's skills that makes the difference.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.390
Yes, yes.

00:19:30.430 --> 00:19:31.270
You!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.650
With the flowers!

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.730
I'm happy you remember me.

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:36.690
My name is Sela D. Miranda.

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:41.240
You showed some good moves for a second there, but didn't pan out.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.700
I'm pretty disappointed.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:43.450
What?!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.620
Did you slip a bit in prison?

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.780
Dunk Mask was different.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.160
When you started dribbling in the stadium,

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.920
my heart started to pound; it truly did.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:03.630
When you destroyed the stadium, I thought "He's it. He's the one!"

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.220
But that was nipped in the bud.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:07.050
In that moment, you were already over.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:09.470
You know what a legend is?

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.100
It's a story that has ended.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.750
It doesn't have any future.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:15.080
Bye bye, Dunk Mask.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.750
I've got no more reason to bother with you.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:19.230
O-Over?

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.940
No more reason?

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.700
Wait a second!

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:29.200
What are they?

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:29.950
Shells? {alt tl: Bombs?}

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:31.100
No, it's different!

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.080
A ball?

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.340
Wait... Dunk Mask?

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:46.550
What are you gonna do?

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.350
What are you doing, stupid-head?! {lit: stupid dumpling}

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.060
If that hit you in the head, you'd get even stupider!

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:53.020
Shut up!

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:55.560
I'll be damned if I'm gonna let an opponent turn
 his back on me when I can't even see his face!

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.480
So will you promise to run away once you see his face?!

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.820
I'll decide that after I get a look!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.280
You'll die! We're gonna die!

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:15.120
Dan's legend is pretty popular, isn't it?

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:17.200
But we don't know how long that'll last!

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:19.290
In business, the ones who move
 fast and get there first win!

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.700
Step right up, step right up!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.590
We've got your Dunk Mask merchandise right here!

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.330
Next time: Destroy, Destroy

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:27.120
NEXT TIME

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:27.120
DESTROY

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:27.120
DESTROY

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.230
Oops! Here comes the legend!
